---
import handoffDark from "../assets/crops/handoff-card-dark.png";
import handoff from "../assets/crops/handoff-card.png";
import handoffPhoneDark from "@media/phone/phone-10-handoff-dark.png";
import handoffPhone from "@media/phone/phone-10-handoff.png";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Shot from "./Shot.astro";
import Video from "./Video.astro";
---

<Section id="computer" eyebrow="Your cloud computer" title="Work on a desktop you can watch and control.">
  <p slot="lede" class="mt-6 text-lede text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
    In your own deployment, each user has a cloud computer: a Linux desktop. Its files stay between jobs. The agent runs
    code and uses apps on it. You can watch it work, press Control to use it, and Release it back.
  </p>

  <!-- From lg, two tiles of one shape side by side, so the captions line up. The 5 % padding is of the width, so the
       956 x 726 loop fills the first tile exactly: 0.1 + 0.9 x 726 / 956 = 749 / 956. Below lg each tile hugs its
       content, and under 640 px the screen loop drops the padding to use the full column. -->
  <div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-14 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <figure>
      <div class="frame grid aspect-[956/749] place-items-center p-[5%] max-sm:aspect-auto max-sm:p-0">
        <div class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-background shadow-composer">
          <Video name="screen-control" dark="screen-control-dark" label="Control of the screen: a typed command prints a table, then Release" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Control and Release</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-[34rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          The screen streams live to your device. Press Control to use the desktop yourself; the agent's desktop tool stays
          locked until you press Release.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-[34rem] text-[0.8125rem] text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          The web app in a browser, in demo mode. The screen is a bare X session streamed from agentd, not the VM image's Xfce desktop.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <!-- Below lg the card alone, at about its size in the app. From lg the phone's Screen tab on a handoff to the
           same site stands beside it: the sign-in page on the cloud computer, with Done and Cancel. -->
      <div class="frame flex items-center justify-center gap-[5%] px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:aspect-[956/749] lg:p-[5%]">
        <div class="hidden w-[34%] shrink-0 lg:block">
          <div class="rounded-[1.6rem] bg-[#151412] p-[5px] shadow-composer dark:bg-black dark:ring-1 dark:ring-white/12">
            <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[1.3rem]">
              <Shot
                src={handoffPhone}
                dark={handoffPhoneDark}
                alt="The web app at phone size on a handoff: the reports site's sign-in page, with Done and Cancel"
                widths={[160, 320, 480]}
                sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 170px, 14vw"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="w-full max-w-[384px] rounded-xl bg-background p-1 shadow-composer lg:max-w-none lg:flex-1">
          <Shot
            src={handoff}
            dark={handoffDark}
            alt="A handoff card: Sign in to the reports site, with Done and Cancel"
            widths={[384, 768]}
            sizes="384px"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Handoffs</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-[34rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          On a sign-in page, a code request or a captcha, the agent is told to stop. It hands you the screen. You sign in
          on your cloud computer, press Done, and the job goes on. The agent is told never to solve a captcha.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-[34rem] text-[0.8125rem] text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          The web app in a browser, in demo mode: the card at desktop width<span class="max-lg:hidden">, the Screen tab
          at phone size in a drawn frame</span>.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Section>
